    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-4519",
      "problem": "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130155/assets/08a20165c8f65b5c5f31e8015eedcec1baa10c3bd70d0964a640aee98dab3ea3.svg)\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130155/assets/143c9c6e7fdb3772f1ad4b44ce5461893ca5b99ce0a72b7ec41b5d78db8643f8.svg)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130155/assets/ee6b50d3e909fb379649c9859124b6633319008d978cb94940828659c29152ee.svg)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130155/assets/bf8ebfa7ea9ec71d8cad0c8effb986eb734179b2e5aa208ae8bc6afd231d90ba.svg)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130155/assets/03124c054d9c5de6d00cf7404d2ef1ea17cc5174d3a743d318f323963c39bd93.svg)\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$",
